1
00:00:00,079 --> 00:00:01,831
Sometimes citizens think,

2
00:00:01,831 --> 00:00:05,918
“Oh, this is my personal problem or a personal issue.

3
00:00:05,918 --> 00:00:10,339
So it’s kind of a waste of time to speak up.”

4
00:00:10,339 --> 00:00:12,008
But this is not true.

5
00:00:12,008 --> 00:00:17,346
If someone speaks up and others agree with it,

6
00:00:17,346 --> 00:00:21,517
that personal issue becomes social issue.

7
00:00:21,517 --> 00:00:23,478
With my administration,

8
00:00:23,478 --> 00:00:28,274
the city government actually did not make a town vision.

9
00:00:28,274 --> 00:00:33,571
Instead of that, citizens created the vision by themselves

10
00:00:33,571 --> 00:00:38,534
and we, local government, supported the process,

11
00:00:38,534 --> 00:00:42,747
because [a] city is citizens --

12
00:00:42,747 --> 00:00:46,250
[a] city is not the government.

13
00:00:46,250 --> 00:00:48,002
I am Takashima Ryosuke,

14
00:00:48,002 --> 00:00:50,588
the youngest mayor in Japanese history.

15
00:00:50,588 --> 00:00:53,466
I’m the mayor of Ashiya City.

16
00:00:53,466 --> 00:00:57,220
(Speaking in Japanese)

17
00:00:57,220 --> 00:00:59,931
I’m a mayor, but I’m not a politician.

18
00:00:59,931 --> 00:01:03,059
My stance is actually very simple.

19
00:01:03,059 --> 00:01:07,313
I just listen to as many voices as possible,

20
00:01:07,313 --> 00:01:09,273
especially (from) younger generations.

21
00:01:09,273 --> 00:01:11,150
The reason is very simple:

22
00:01:11,150 --> 00:01:15,530
students under 18 cannot vote.

23
00:01:15,530 --> 00:01:17,281
So I visited schools,

24
00:01:17,281 --> 00:01:19,784
like junior high schools and elementary schools,

25
00:01:19,784 --> 00:01:21,828
to hear their voices.

26
00:01:21,828 --> 00:01:27,583
But it’s so hard for kids, for students, to speak their opinions to a mayor --

27
00:01:27,583 --> 00:01:30,336
even if I am the youngest mayor.

28
00:01:30,336 --> 00:01:36,592
So what I did was eat school lunch together,

29
00:01:36,592 --> 00:01:40,763
and I repeatedly visited schools.

30
00:01:40,763 --> 00:01:44,433
I didn’t want to be a formal visit,

31
00:01:44,433 --> 00:01:46,477
but rather a casual visit,

32
00:01:46,477 --> 00:01:50,523
casual chat with teachers and students.

33
00:01:50,523 --> 00:01:54,610
I could create the kind of friendly atmosphere,

34
00:01:54,610 --> 00:01:59,740
and I got more information rather than [in] a formal visit.

35
00:01:59,740 --> 00:02:05,454
For example, some students told me their school gym was so hot.

36
00:02:05,454 --> 00:02:10,251
So we decided to install air conditioners

37
00:02:10,251 --> 00:02:13,462
in every single school gym.

38
00:02:13,462 --> 00:02:18,718
I wanted to make schools a place to learn and practice democracy.

39
00:02:18,718 --> 00:02:22,763
And it's all about communication and dialogue.

40
00:02:22,763 --> 00:02:28,186
I wanted to encourage people to speak up, listen to their voices,

41
00:02:28,186 --> 00:02:30,938
and then reflect their voices.

42
00:02:30,938 --> 00:02:35,151
The main method is holding dialogue meetings.

43
00:02:35,151 --> 00:02:39,530
It’s a meeting with me, mayor, and citizens

44
00:02:39,530 --> 00:02:43,117
sit down together in a circle and talk with each other.

45
00:02:43,117 --> 00:02:48,039
And sometimes the mayor does not even speak up.

46
00:02:48,039 --> 00:02:54,086
Just listens or facilitates what citizens want to talk about.

47
00:02:54,086 --> 00:02:58,674
So, for example, Ashiya is a very healthy city.

48
00:02:58,674 --> 00:03:03,930
Recently, we had the world's oldest person in Ashiya city.

49
00:03:03,930 --> 00:03:08,309
Around 30 percent of the citizens are over 65.

50
00:03:08,309 --> 00:03:09,560
In the dialogue meetings,

51
00:03:09,560 --> 00:03:13,981
I heard elderly people say that the community centers were too busy

52
00:03:13,981 --> 00:03:16,859
to answer their questions about care.

53
00:03:16,859 --> 00:03:20,613
So I wanted to increase the number of community centers,

54
00:03:20,613 --> 00:03:22,740
but we needed some budget.

55
00:03:22,740 --> 00:03:25,326
So before we had a monetary gift for elderly people,

56
00:03:25,326 --> 00:03:28,996
so we decided to change our monetary gift system,

57
00:03:28,996 --> 00:03:30,581
from a one-time monetary gift

58
00:03:30,581 --> 00:03:33,376
to creating [a] new community center

59
00:03:33,376 --> 00:03:36,045
where elderly people and their families

60
00:03:36,045 --> 00:03:39,298
get some advice on wellness.

61
00:03:39,298 --> 00:03:43,844
Some people say monetary gifts are a kind of symbol of respect.

62
00:03:43,844 --> 00:03:45,513
So some people argued

63
00:03:45,513 --> 00:03:49,976
that I had no respect for elderly people.

64
00:03:49,976 --> 00:03:51,686
But through the dialogue sessions,

65
00:03:51,686 --> 00:03:54,981
I explained why this was important

66
00:03:54,981 --> 00:04:00,611
and why this actually benefited for elderly people.

67
00:04:00,611 --> 00:04:05,658
And I also cut my future monetary gift.

68
00:04:05,658 --> 00:04:09,203
So this was not like others’ problem;

69
00:04:09,203 --> 00:04:11,372
this was our problem.

70
00:04:11,372 --> 00:04:15,543
Finally, they (came to) understand why we needed to change.

71
00:04:15,543 --> 00:04:22,717
They changed their opinion because they understood the process.

72
00:04:22,717 --> 00:04:27,054
During cherry blossom season, when cherry blossoms bloom beautifully,

73
00:04:27,054 --> 00:04:30,558
local shops wanted to close the street

74
00:04:30,558 --> 00:04:34,520
to enjoy food under the cherry blossoms.

75
00:04:34,520 --> 00:04:38,858
But for local residents, that proposal was simply inconvenient,

76
00:04:38,858 --> 00:04:41,277
so it was controversial.

77
00:04:41,277 --> 00:04:47,908
But when local citizens and local shops actually joined the process

78
00:04:47,908 --> 00:04:51,245
and citizens proposed the plan,

79
00:04:51,245 --> 00:04:54,081
the proposal was a success.

80
00:04:54,081 --> 00:04:58,669
So citizens actually created the vision of (our) town,

81
00:04:58,669 --> 00:05:00,963
not the government.

82
00:05:00,963 --> 00:05:02,590
People tend to think

83
00:05:02,590 --> 00:05:06,385
that the ones who make society better are the government

84
00:05:06,385 --> 00:05:08,346
or someone else.

85
00:05:08,346 --> 00:05:10,431
and not ourselves.

86
00:05:10,431 --> 00:05:13,100
I want to change that mindset.

87
00:05:13,100 --> 00:05:15,061
It is everyone.

88
00:05:15,061 --> 00:05:18,481
It's every single person who can make society better

89
00:05:18,481 --> 00:05:21,484
and who can contribute to making society better.

90
00:05:21,484 --> 00:05:26,864
That is what I want to do.

91
00:05:26,864 --> 00:05:30,864
Thank you.
